-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- Seed: ingredient (bahan baku) stock + recipes for every existing menu item
-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
--
-- Every menu item across both branches previously had no linked ingredients
-- (menu_ingredients had exactly one stray test row), so the Kitchen ->
-- Inventory deduction path (kitchen_inventory_service.dart) never ran and the
-- Inventory screen's low-stock alert had nothing realistic to show. This seeds:
--   1. inventory_items: one row per ingredient per branch, dated TODAY (the
--      table is date-scoped daily -- see rolloverDailyStock -- so a row with
--      an old date is invisible to fetchInventoryItems()'s `eq('date', today)`
--      filter). Stock levels are intentionally mixed: most ingredients are
--      comfortably stocked, a few are deliberately BELOW minimum_stock (low
--      stock) or at 0 (out of stock) on each branch, so the low-stock alert UI
--      has real data to display instead of an empty state.
--   2. menu_ingredients: a recipe (ingredient + qty per portion) for every one
--      of the 16 menu items x 2 branches, matching this project's existing
--      Indonesian-cuisine menu. Quantities are a reasonable per-portion
--      estimate (assistant judgment, not a real recipe spec).
--
-- The one pre-existing menu_ingredients row (Ayam Bakar -> Telur, 0.1666kg --
-- a leftover from manual testing, and not a sensible pairing) is removed so it
-- doesn't sit alongside this seed as a duplicate/contradictory recipe line.
-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

delete from public.menu_ingredients
  where id = '890551a1-bd2f-4382-90ec-704d1e16beb0';

